15 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a nanoparticle tracking analysis graph with particle concentration peaks labeled at 92, 105, and 200 nanometers. Panel B is a box plot comparing extracellular vesicle \(EV\) numbers per milliliter plasma between PASC-negative and PASC-positive groups, marked as not significant. Panel C is a bar graph comparing EV number per microgram protein between groups, also labeled not significant. Panel D presents Western blot results for exosome markers CD9, Alix, CD81, IntegrinB1, TSG101, and CD63, showing bands at their respective molecular weights for PASC samples.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a heatmap depicting hierarchical clustering of expression values for multiple genes across two groups, PASC.Neg \(green\) and PASC.Pos \(magenta\), with a blue-to-red scale representing lower to higher expression. Panel B displays a volcano plot of gene expression data, plotting log2 fold change versus negative log10 P-value, highlighting significant genes in different colors with labels for selected genes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Four grouped bar charts displaying pathway enrichment analysis: Panel A shows KEGG enrichment, Panel B GO biological process enrichment, Panel C Reactome enrichment, and Panel D IPA pathway enrichment. Each panel lists enriched pathways or processes on the left and their -log10\(p value\) on the x-axis, with highest values for immune, cytokine, apoptotic, and coagulation-related pathways.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a treemap visualizing biological and disease categories with colored squares indicating statistical significance and z-scores based on a blue-to-orange scale, labeled by categories such as cancer, immunological disease, and gastrointestinal disease. Panel B presents a blue-tinted Voronoi diagram subdivided into various biological processes and systems, such as immunity, signal transduction, cell cycle, and metabolism, with subdivisions for related sub-processes and pathways.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a series of box plots for genes grouped by thrombosis, apoptosis/cell cycle/proliferation, complement, and inflammation, comparing two groups with p-values and gene names labeled above each plot. Panel B contains network diagrams for each gene category, illustrating gene interactions and associations within thrombosis, cell cycle, complement, and inflammation networks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Figure presents two grouped bar graph panels comparing four groups\204Acute, PASC positive, PASC negative, and Donor\204for four analytes: FN1, HCF-H, HGF, and IL17RA in EVs \(panel A\) and plasma \(panel B\). Significant differences are marked with asterisks and \215ns\216 for non-significant comparisons; y-axis values indicate concentration. Individual data points are visible for each bar.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
